cl. 1. P. क्वणति (pr. p. क्वणत्), to sound, make any sound, tinkle, Amar.; Kathās. lxxxv, 25; Hit.;
to hum (as a bee), Bhaṭṭ. vi, 84;
 (said of Kiṃnaras and Yātu-dhānas), Kum. i, 55 and Bhaṭṭ. (aor. 3. pl. अक्वाणिषुर्) :
Caus. P. क्वणयति (pr. p. f. ˚यती), to cause to sound, make sound (as a musical instrument), blow (the flute), BhP. iii, 15, 21; x, 44, 13 and 16;
to produce a sound with (instr.), iv, 24, 12; x, 60, 8.

cl. 1. Ā. क्वथते, to boil, prepare by heat, Kāṭh.;
to digest, W.;
to be hot (as the heart), Hcar. :
Caus. क्वाथयति, to cause to boil, decoct, Kauś.; ŚārṅgS.;
 (Pass. क्वाथ्यते), MBh.; Suśr. i, 45, 3; MārkP. xii, 36.
